From: FingerBrowser
Subject: [PATCH 0013] WebRTC IP handling to stop real-IP leak

The WebRTC IP handling policy shipped as a no-op: the browser process
appended --force-webrtc-ip-handling-policy, which nothing in this build
consumes, so WebRTC kept gathering a STUN reflexive candidate that leaked the
host's real public IP even when HTTP traffic exited through a proxy in
another country -- a US HTTP IP next to a China WebRTC IP.

The policy is actually read as a renderer preference populated from a pref
the command line never sets. This adds an fp-webrtc-ip-policy switch, sends
it to the renderer, and reads it in PeerConnectionDependencyFactory to force
the policy (e.g. disable_non_proxied_udp) before it maps to port-allocator
flags. With the policy applied WebRTC yields no IP candidates at all.

Depends on: 0001-0012.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_policy.cc b/chrome/browser/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_policy.cc
index f0e4470d59..02dcc7c752 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_policy.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_policy.cc
@@ -326,7 +326,11 @@ void ApplyFingerBrowserPolicy(const FingerBrowserPolicy& policy,
     command_line->AppendSwitch(permissions::switches::kDenyPermissionPrompts);
   }
   if (policy.webrtc_ip_policy != "default") {
-    command_line->AppendSwitchASCII(switches::kForceWebRtcIPHandlingPolicy,
+    // switches::kForceWebRtcIPHandlingPolicy is not consumed anywhere in this
+    // build, so passing it did nothing and WebRTC kept leaking the real IP.
+    // Send a dedicated fp switch that the peer-connection factory reads in the
+    // renderer instead.
+    command_line->AppendSwitchASCII("fp-webrtc-ip-policy",
                                     policy.webrtc_ip_policy);
   }
 
diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
index bb46e773e8..3821414393 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
@@ -3390,6 +3390,7 @@ void RenderProcessHostImpl::PropagateBrowserCommandLineToRenderer(
       "fp-screen-height",
       "fp-geo-lat-e6",
       "fp-geo-lon-e6",
+      "fp-webrtc-ip-policy",
       switches::kDisableInProcessStackTraces,
       sandbox::policy::switches::kDisableSeccompFilterSandbox,
       sandbox::policy::switches::kNoSandbox,
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/peer_connection_dependency_factory.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/peer_connection_dependency_factory.cc
index fd6ce5a7f0..ab492efa6b 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/peer_connection_dependency_factory.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/peer_connection_dependency_factory.cc
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 #include "net/net_buildflags.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/public/common/features.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/public/common/peerconnection/webrtc_ip_handling_policy.h"
+#include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_fingerprint.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/public/platform/modules/webrtc/webrtc_logging.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/public/platform/platform.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/public/platform/task_type.h"
@@ -834,6 +835,16 @@ PeerConnectionDependencyFactory::CreatePortAllocator(
       // |request_multiple_routes|. Whether local IP addresses could be
       // collected depends on if mic/camera permission is granted for this
       // origin.
+      // FingerBrowser: the IP handling policy normally arrives via a renderer
+      // preference populated from the kWebRTCIPHandlingPolicy pref, which our
+      // browser-process command line never sets. Force it from our own switch
+      // so WebRTC honours the profile's policy (e.g. disable_non_proxied_udp)
+      // instead of falling back to kDefault and leaking the host's real IP.
+      if (const std::string fb_webrtc = fingerbrowser::SwitchValue(
+              fingerbrowser::kWebRtcIpPolicySwitch);
+          !fb_webrtc.empty()) {
+        webrtc_ip_handling_policy = WebString::FromUTF8(fb_webrtc);
+      }
       WebRTCIPHandlingPolicy policy =
           GetWebRTCIPHandlingPolicy(webrtc_ip_handling_policy);
       switch (policy) {
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_fingerprint.h b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_fingerprint.h
index 7b7225f344..edf91355f4 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_fingerprint.h
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_fingerprint.h
@@ -52,6 +52,18 @@ inline constexpr char kDoNotTrackSwitch[] = "fp-do-not-track";
 inline constexpr char kGeoLatitudeE6Switch[] = "fp-geo-lat-e6";
 inline constexpr char kGeoLongitudeE6Switch[] = "fp-geo-lon-e6";
 
+// WebRTC IP handling policy (e.g. "disable_non_proxied_udp"). This must be a
+// renderer switch, not just a pref: Chromium reads the policy from a renderer
+// preference (webrtc_ip_handling_policy) that is populated from the
+// kWebRTCIPHandlingPolicy pref, and the browser-process command line never
+// sets that pref -- so the renderer sees an empty string, falls back to
+// kDefault, and enable_nonproxied_udp stays true. The result is a STUN
+// reflexive candidate that leaks the host's real public IP even when HTTP
+// traffic exits through a proxy in another country. Reading this switch
+// directly in the peer-connection factory forces the policy regardless of the
+// pref plumbing.
+inline constexpr char kWebRtcIpPolicySwitch[] = "fp-webrtc-ip-policy";
+
 // WebGPU adapter identity. Separate from the WebGL switches because the two
 // APIs use different vocabularies: WebGL reports "Google Inc. (NVIDIA)" and an
 // ANGLE renderer string, while WebGPU reports lowercase tokens ("nvidia",
